# Apex app paths — owner decision 2026-08-08: nikatru.com/<app> is the permanent
# public address for an app's commerce/product surface, so Paddle domain approval
# is a one-time act on the apex, never a per-app submission. The path serves the
# hub's per-app page today; the checkout increment upgrades it. That increment is
# gated by paywall.enabled=false (services/platform/src/app-config-data.json) plus
# OWNER_QUEUE A-1 -- NOT by OD-6.1, which CLOSED AS SUPERSEDED on 2026-08-08 (see
# knowledge/decisions/036-subly-freeze-dissolved-by-owner-order.md). This line named
# OD-6.1 as an open gate until 2026-08-11. sites/ sat outside that ADR's own declared
# citation sweep (company/pipeline/* and knowledge/), which is exactly why it survived.
# Precision, because a records file that overstates is the defect it is fixing: this
# file is public in the REPO but is never SERVED -- Cloudflare consumes _redirects and
# assert-web-cache-policy.mjs:168 lists it NOT_SERVED. pricing.html, repaired the same
# day, is the one whose comment shipped the stale gate id to every browser.
/subly /apps/subly.html 301
/subly/ /apps/subly.html 301
